# The SECOND `parallel for` refusal, locked byte-for-byte as
# tests/diag/parfor_expr_source.err. Sibling of tests/diag/dotlt_sequential.ty,
# which pins the three-clause message one arm over: this one is the
# foreach-of-an-expression arm, reached when the source of a
# `parallel for x in EXPR` is not an identifier. It was asserted by nothing
# before this fixture -- `grep -rn "must name a variable" tests docs src` found it
# only in src/tychoc.c and a prose mention in docs/guides/concurrency.md:102, and
# a tests/reject/ case would have accepted any nonzero exit with any message.
# What the message has to keep saying is the FIX ("bind it first"), because the
# refusal is not about the expression being wrong -- both an array and a channel
# source are scalar handles, so the parser needs a name it can re-read rather than
# an eval-once temp a channel cannot safely be aliased into. Refused at
# src/tychoc.c:3633.
fn build() -> [int]:
    a := []int
    push(a, 1)
    push(a, 2)
    return a

fn main():
    total := 0
    parallel for v in build():
        total += v
    print(str(total))
